      "id": 1,
      "text": "The first apple orchard opened in 1876 by Enoch Parrish, followed by the Wilshire family.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oak_Glen%2C_San_Bernardino_County%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Rivers brothers founded Los Rios Rancho in 1906, and it remains Southern California’s largest historic ranch.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oak_Glen%2C_San_Bernardino_County%2C_California",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Los Rios Rancho draws more than 300,000 visitors yearly, offering apple picking and historic tours.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oak_Glen%2C_San_Bernardino_County%2C_California",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the 1940s, local farms began selling apples, pies, cider, and butter at roadside stands, sparking Oak Glen’s apple boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oak_Glen%2C_San_Bernardino_County%2C_California",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Wildlands Conservancy acquired Los Rios Rancho in 1996 and opened Oak Glen Preserve, adding hiking trails and picnic areas.",
